The desktop main process tried to scrape the session token out of
`GET /` (the SPA index), but the headless `wenshu serve` backend has
no SPA mount — the path 404s with
"Headless backend (wenshu serve): web UI disabled" and the token was
never adopted. Spawn-time `WENSHU_DASHBOARD_SESSION_TOKEN` differs
when the backend regenerates the value, so /api/ws 401s and the
composer sticks on "Could not connect to 文枢 gateway".

- apps/desktop/electron/dashboard-token.ts: read `authToken` from the
  public /api/status JSON body. The endpoint is in PUBLIC_API_PATHS on
  every bind, so the new path works against the headless `serve`
  backend and the legacy `dashboard` equally. /api/status is also
  the liveness probe, so the JSON fetch is one round-trip for both
  readiness and token pickup.
- wenshu_cli/web_server.py::get_status: include `_SESSION_TOKEN`
  as `authToken` in the loopback-mode body (the gated mode already
  uses cookie auth and must NOT leak the legacy token).
- apps/desktop/electron/main.ts: stamp each finalize step
  (window.show / wsUrl mount / bootProgress dismiss) so a stuck boot
  surfaces a deterministic last-successful line in the log instead of
  dying silently at phase backend.ready.
- apps/desktop/electron/dashboard-token.test.ts: rewrite to cover
  the /api/status JSON path (legacy HTML-scrape tests removed).
- Build: dist electron-main.mjs + mac-arm64 文枢-0.0.1.dmg rebuilt
  (also archived as .dmg.r28). Pytest not run locally (no pytest in
  PATH), so test_web_server.py::test_get_status is unverified; the
  contract it pins (authToken in body) is verified via FastAPI
  TestClient smoke test in this commit message.

AC list:
- AC1: dashboard-token.ts reads /api/status (not /)
- AC2: wenshu_cli /api/status returns authToken in loopback mode
- AC3: desktop .app + .dmg rebuilt with R34 changes
- AC4: TestClient smoke test confirms /api/status -> 200, authToken
  present, matches _SESSION_TOKEN; gated mode correctly omits token
- AC5: commit + push + 装机 user notify (Feishu DM via PM)
